# [WEB-THEME-1 2026-08-26] …but NOT the web client's design tokens. `design/`
# above is a bare pattern, so it also matched `web/design/`, where
# `zine-tokens.dart` lives — the single source of truth that
# `scripts/export-zine-tokens.mjs` compiles into tokens.css and the Tailwind
# theme on every build (`npm run prebuild`). The file was already tracked, so
# nothing was lost, but `git add` refused every edit to it: the one file that
# controls the site's entire palette could not be committed by normal means.
!web/design/
!web/design/**

# [DESIGN-PREVIEW-1 2026-08-26] …and NOT the live-streaming mockups, which are
# now tracked so `design-preview.yml` can publish them to the `avatok-design`
# Pages project. CI checks out the repo — an ignored file is a file CI cannot
# deploy, which is the only reason these moved into git.
#
# Only the ~7MB that actually RENDERS is tracked: the .dc.html pages, the
# support.js runtime, README.md and assets/. Deliberately still ignored, because
# no page references any of it: uploads/ (26MB of raw drops),
# design_handoff_avatok_auth/, _src/, .thumbnail and the .jsx device frames.
#
# `design/` on line 171 excludes the DIRECTORY, and git will not descend into an
# excluded directory — so a bare `!design/live-streaming/**` does nothing. The
# parent has to be re-included first, then its other children re-excluded. Hence
# the alternating negations below; do not "simplify" them into one line.
!design/
/design/*
!/design/live-streaming/
/design/live-streaming/*
!/design/live-streaming/*.dc.html
!/design/live-streaming/index.html
!/design/live-streaming/support.js
!/design/live-streaming/README.md
!/design/live-streaming/assets/
!/design/live-streaming/assets/**

# [DEMO-LISTING-1 2026-08-26] Build output, not source. web/scripts/copy-design-demo.mjs
# regenerates web/public/demo/ from design/live-streaming/ on every build and dev
# run. Committing it would be a second 7MB copy of the same PNGs, free to drift.
web/public/demo/
tools/

